{"body":"This PR changes `drizzle-kit/payload/postgres` and `drizzle-kit/payload/sqlite` for the asks in #6689 and for Payload's feedback on delta snapshots. It changes existing signatures and adds no new exports.

```ts
// Postgres. `prev` is the state of the last migration, or nothing for the first one.
const { snapshots } = await up(files);              // one-time: full states -> base + diff snapshots
const prev = await reconstruct(snapshots);
const { sqlStatements, snapshot, hints } = await generateMigration(prev, await generateDrizzleJson(schema), {
  hints: knownHints,
  interactive: true,                                 // prompts like the CLI when stdin is a TTY
  createSchemaIfNotExists: true,
});

// SQLite and Postgres push
const { sqlStatements, warnings, hints, apply } = await pushSchema(schema, db, entitiesFilter, migrations, options);
```

- Delta snapshots (Postgres): `generateMigration` returns the snapshot of the migration with the SQL. The snapshot is a `base` snapshot for the first migration and a `diff` snapshot with deltas and footprints after that, as `generate` writes them. `up(files)` converts a folder of full states of format 7 to 10 to one base snapshot and diff snapshots, and it returns a converted folder unchanged. `reconstruct` says what to do when it gets a full state.
- Ask 1: `generateMigration` and `pushSchema` take `interactive`. With a TTY on stdin, rename-or-create questions prompt as in the CLI. Without one, the option has no effect. Interactive `pushSchema` returns the data loss items in `warnings` and does not ask about them, so the caller co","headRefName":"payload-delta-snapshots","state":"OPEN","title":"Change the payload postgres and sqlite APIs for Payload CMS","url":"https://github.com/drizzle-team/drizzle-orm/pull/6696"}

{"body":"# v1.0.0-rc.6

# drizzle-orm

## Breaking changes

- Drivers no longer configure output decoding in drivers' configurations - following configurations set by drizzle constructors were removed:
  - `client.options.bigint = true` from `bun-sql/postgres`, `bun-sql/mysql`
  - transparent decoders from `postgres-js`
  - global `types.setTypeParser(...)` from `neon-http`, `netlify-db`
  - per-query parser overrides from `raw` mode and other queries not decoded by codecs (`node-postgres`, `node-postgres/dsql`, `vercel-postgres`, `neon-serverless`, `netlify-db`, `cockroach`, `pglite`, `mysql2`)

  :exclamation:`postgres-js` still overrides client's param serializers (client-wide, replacing user-configured ones) for `timestamptz` (`1184`), `timestamp` (`1114`), `date` (`1082`), `time` (`1083`) and their arrays:
  - `Date` values are sent as `value.toISOString()` - same as `postgres.js`' default for `timestamptz`, `timestamp`, `date`
  - strings are sent as is to be parsed by the server - `postgres.js`' default re-encodes them via `new Date(value).toISOString()`, which reads offset-less timestamps in process' local time, truncates microseconds and throws on values JS can't parse (`'infinity'`, `'12:00:00'`)
  - `time` switches `Date` processing from `date.toString()` to ISO string

  `sqlite`: integer-based codecs (`integer`, `integer:boolean`, `integer:timestamp`, `integer:timestamp_ms`) accept `number`, `bigint` and integer text, which makes them independent of safe integer modes (`better-sqlite3`'s `defaultSafeIntegers`, `bun:sqlite`'s `safeIntegers`, `node:sqlite","headRefName":"rc6","state":"MERGED","title":"rc5 fixes","url":"https://github.com/drizzle-team/drizzle-orm/pull/6588"}
